    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0534" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg454"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Prince
                            Oblensky.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                            1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received through Mr. Wollant your excellency’s touching message of
                    condolence on the part of the Imperial Government. In the name of the American
                    people and their Government I thank you for this fraternal proof of sympathy
                    from a nation so long friendly and so highly esteemed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
